=== SCHEMA ===

migrations/000160_vehicle_unit_history.up.sql
---------------------------------------------
Authored exactly per the prompt's spec:

  * id BIGSERIAL — monotonic tiebreaker for same-instant inserts.
    Required by ADR-004 #4: bootstrap (time.Now()) and telemetry
    (atomic.EmittedAt) can collide at the same effective_from second,
    and without a deterministic tiebreaker two pods can resolve
    different "active" units for the same t. The composite ORDER BY
    (effective_from DESC, id DESC) at lookup time guarantees
    consistency.
  * vehicle_id BIGINT NOT NULL.
  * unit_kind TEXT NOT NULL with CHECK constraint to
    {distance, temperature, pressure, charge}.
  * unit_value TEXT NOT NULL — the units.ActiveUnit string form so
    the column round-trips through Go without a mapping table.
  * effective_from TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL — wall-clock UTC for every
    consumer in this pipeline.
  * source TEXT NOT NULL with CHECK constraint to
    {telemetry, rest_bootstrap, manual} so accidental writes from
    UI-preference paths fail at insert time.
  * PRIMARY KEY (vehicle_id, unit_kind, effective_from, id) — gives
    the supporting index the prefix it needs and includes id for
    uniqueness on collisions.
  * UNIQUE (vehicle_id, unit_kind, effective_from, unit_value, source)
    — idempotency contract. Paired with ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING in
    repo.go, this makes telemetry replays and bootstrap re-runs no-op
    inserts.
  * CREATE INDEX vehicle_unit_history_lookup
      ON (vehicle_id, unit_kind, effective_from DESC, id DESC) — the
    DESC composite mirrors the ORDER BY in the lookup SQL exactly so
    the planner resolves the entire query as an index-only backward
    scan that stops at the first row.
  * COMMENT ON TABLE documenting the ADR-004 reference and the
    "NEVER use as the source of UI display preferences" warning.

